o}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T07:54:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T16:34:42Z","body":"Oh I see sorry, I misunderstood what the margins are supposed to do. With this new perspective some concerns that are hopefully more valid:\r\n- I think this behavior would be easier to understand if the scroll bars didn't shrink with the margins as their default behavior (`scrollbar_margin_* = 0` would be better). For me scroll bars intuitively show the bounds of the scrolled content\r\n- When `column_titles_visible` is enabled the top margin will actually be cut off. Maybe it would be better if it sticks to the first entry until it reaches the top of the container\r\n\r\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/02c064b8-e7d8-4697-ae27-e5cf83686e0b\" />\r\n\r\n- When both scroll bars are visible the content overlaps with them\r\n\r\n<img height=\"300\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/92c5245d-cf22-4931-8bc9-434091e88fa2\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5436074793/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]